is expression:\n\\[\n(b^4 + b^3 + b + 1) \\cdot (b-1) = b^5 - b^4 + b^4 - b^3 + b^2 - b + b - 1 = b^5 - b^3 + b^2 - 1\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Convert $1001_b$ to base-10.\nThe base-$b$ number $1001_b$ can be expressed in base-10 as:\n\\[\n1 \\cdot b^3 + 0 \\cdot b^2 + 0 \\cdot b + 1 = b^3 + 1\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Add $1001_b$ (in base-10) to the result from Step 2.\n\\[\nb^5 - b^3 + b^2 - 1 + b^3 + 1 = b^5 + b^2\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Convert $b^5 + b^2$ back to base-$b$.\nThe expression $b^5 + b^2$ can be directly written in base-$b$ as:\n\\[\n100100_b\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{100100_b}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{100100_b}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
